<title>HONG KONG: Orient Overseas 1996 net rises 68 pct.</title>
<headline>Orient Overseas 1996 net rises 68 pct.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1997-04-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year ended December 31</p>
<p>(in millions US$ unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr (U.S. cents)	  21.7     vs 12.2</p>
<p>    Dividend (U.S. cents)   1.60     vs 1.28</p>
<p>    Exceptional items	 57.72    vs 2.44</p>
<p>    Net			   109.45   vs 65.21</p>
<p>    Turnover		    1,882.32 vs 1,671.63</p>
<p>    Company name		Orient Overseas (International) Ltd</p>
<p>    Books close		 May 8-15</p>
<p>    Dividend payable	  May 26</p>
<p>NOTE - Orient Overseas owns and operates container ships and container terminals.</p>
<p>The company said the exceptional gain was profit from sale of vessels.</p>
<p>Total dividend for year is 2.60 U.S. cents (including interim dividend of one cent) vs 2.08 cents.</p>
<p>-- Hong Kong Newsroom (852) 2843 6368</p>
</text>
